# RISC0 Core Component

## Overview
The RISC0 Core component provides foundational utilities and data structures for the RISC0 proof system implementation within the Zirgen framework.

## Location
- **Path**: `risc0/core/`
- **Build**: `BUILD.bazel`

## Key Components

### ELF Module (`elf.cpp`, `elf.h`)
- Handles ELF (Executable and Linkable Format) file parsing and processing
- Critical for loading and analyzing RISC-V executable binaries
- Used in the proof generation pipeline for guest program execution

### Logging System (`log.cpp`, `log.h`)
- Provides structured logging capabilities across the RISC0 system
- Supports different log levels and structured output
- Essential for debugging and monitoring proof generation

### Utilities (`util.cpp`, `util.h`)
- Core utility functions shared across the RISC0 implementation
- Common data structures and helper functions
- Performance-critical low-level operations

### Source Location Tracking (`source_loc.h`)
- Provides source code location tracking for debugging
- Used throughout the system for error reporting and diagnostics
- Helps with tracing issues back to specific code locations

## Testing
- **Test Directory**: `test/`
- **Main Test Runner**: `gtest_main.cpp`
- **User Mode Tests**: `usermode.cpp`

## Dependencies
- Uses Bazel build system
- Integrates with Google Test framework for testing
- Part of the larger Zirgen compiler infrastructure

## Usage Context
This core component serves as the foundation for:
- RISC-V program execution simulation
- Proof generation for RISC0 zkVM
- Integration with the broader Zirgen circuit compilation system
- ELF binary processing for guest programs

## Build Integration
- Uses Bazel BUILD files for compilation
- Integrated with the parent Zirgen build system
- Supports both development and production builds